-- title:
--   Normalized l2 vectors of unit-ball families lie in the unit ball
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a real normed space, $\Omega$ a finite nonempty set, and $f:\Omega\to X$ with $\|f(a)\|\le1$ for all $a$. Then the probability-normalized vector $|\Omega|^{-1/2}f$ in $\ell_2(\Omega;X)$ satisfies
--   $$
--   \bigl\||\Omega|^{-1/2}f\bigr\|=\Bigl(\frac1{|\Omega|}\sum_{a\in\Omega}\|f(a)\|^2\Bigr)^{1/2}\le1 .
--   $$
--
--   This normalization identifies $\ell_2(\Omega;X)$ with $L_2$ of the uniform probability on $\Omega$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/EquivariantPairing.lean#L22-L37

